PM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0019", "ticker": "JPM", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.2835, "filing_name": "JPMorgan Chase & Co 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/000162828026008131/jpm-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0026", "ticker": "JPM", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.2794, "filing_name": "JPMorgan Chase & Co 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/000162828026008131/jpm-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0066", "ticker": "JPM", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.2774, "filing_name": "JPMorgan Chase & Co 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/000162828026008131/jpm-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0030", "ticker": "JPM", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.2768, "filing_name": "JPMorgan Chase & Co 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/000162828026008131/jpm-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 64, "dropped_candidates": 401, "token_estimate": 31392, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "Each company's filing describes a different risk profile. Apple stresses economic conditions, competition, product transitions, outsourced manufacturing and regulatory scrutiny, in its fiscal 2025 10-K for the year ended September 27, 2025 [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0000] [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0008]. Tesla stresses production ramps, new autonomous products such as Cybercab, dependence on Elon Musk, and product liability, in its fiscal 2025 10-K for the year ended December 31, 2025 [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000] [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0018]. JPMorgan leads its fiscal 2025 10-K (year ended December 31, 2025) with legal and regulatory, political, market, and country risks [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000]. Common themes are regulation and litigation, macroeconomic and geopolitical exposure, and cybersecurity or technology risk, while Tesla's and Apple's risks are product- and supply-chain-centered and JPMorgan's are credit-, market- and liquidity-centered [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0023] [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0009]. The filings do not rank their risks, so no ordering by severity is given.", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "AAPL", "company": "Apple Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Operations depend on global and regional economic conditions, with sales outside the U.S. a majority of net sales and most supplier facilities outside the U.S. (fiscal 2025, ended September 27, 2025).", "citations": ["AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0000"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "A significant majority of manufacturing is done by outsourcing partners in Asia, with single-source suppliers for many components, reducing direct control over production.", "citations": ["AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0008", "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0009"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Apple faces intense competition, regulatory and antitrust scrutiny (including App Store investigations and the Google search licensing proceedings), and gross margin pressure.", "citations": ["AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0025", "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0027"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "TSLA", "company": "Tesla Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Tesla's future depends on developing driver assistance and autonomous driving and ramping mass-market vehicles including Cybercab, with past production ramp delays (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "It is highly dependent on Elon Musk, who does not devote full time to Tesla and holds other management positions.", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0019", "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0018"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Tesla faces product liability claims tied to collisions and lithium-ion battery risks, and regulations on autonomous vehicles that may delay Robotaxi expansion.", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0014", "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0034"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "JPM", "company": "JPMorgan Chase & Co", "findings": [{"point": "The principal risk factors summarized are legal and regulatory, political, market, and country risks, among others (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "JPMorgan faces significant legal risk from civil and governmental proceedings, with exposure that could exceed established reserves.", "citations": ["JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0009"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Cybersecurity risks may be intensified by AI and quantum computing, and AI adoption carries competitive and workforce risks.", "citations": ["JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0052", "JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0079"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": {"columns": ["Theme", "Apple (fiscal 2025, ended September 27, 2025)", "Tesla (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025)", "JPMorgan (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025)"], "rows": [["Regulatory/legal", "Antitrust, App Store and complex global laws [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0023]", "Autonomous vehicle rules; privacy law compliance [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0034]", "Proceedings and enforcement actions, heightened oversight [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0009]"], ["Macro/geopolitical", "Economic conditions, trade disputes, tariffs [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0001]", "Rising interest rates may reduce demand [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0008]", "Political developments, tariffs, sanctions [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0020]"], ["Operations/supply", "Outsourced manufacturing, single-source components [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0009]", "Production ramps and factory construction [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0003]", "Data management and systems reliance [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0064]"], ["Technology/cyber", "Quality issues and AI-related safety risks [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0011]", "Cyber-attacks on IT systems [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0019]", "Cyber risk intensified by AI and quantum computing [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0052]"], ["Key-person/strategy", "New ventures may not succeed [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0020]", "Dependence on Elon Musk [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0018]", "Management strategy execution [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0071]"]]}, "citations": [{"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0000", "claim": "Apple macro dependence", "quote": "sales outside the U.S. representing a majority of the Company's total net sales"}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0008", "claim": "Apple outsourced manufacturing", "quote": "A significant majority of the Company's manufacturing is performed in whole or in part by outsourcing partners"}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0009", "claim": "Apple single-source components", "quote": "the Company currently obtains certain components from single or limited sources"}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0023", "claim": "Apple complex global laws", "quote": "The Company is subject to complex and changing laws and regulations worldwide"}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0025", "claim": "Apple regulatory scrutiny", "quote": "intense media, political and regulatory scrutiny"}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025